INSERT INTO `dispute_letters` VALUES (1,42,'TransUnion','Revolving','Multiple','Multiple','Cross-Bureau Discrepancies','Correction or Deletion',1,'Donisha Johnson\n4412 Linecrest Way\nEllenwood, Ga 30294\nDOB: [Enter Date of Birth]\nSSN Last 4: 4187\nPhone: 4703099709\n\nDate: August 11, 2026\n\nTO:\nTransunion Credit Services\nCredit Reporting Agency\nATTN: Disputes Department\nPost Office Box 2000\nChester, PA 19016\n\nRE: NOTICE OF FCRA DISPUTE - INACCURATE REPORTING\n\nDear Disputes Department,\n\nPursuant to the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA), 15 U.S.C. § 1681i (Section 611) and 15 U.S.C. § 1681s-2 (Section 623), I am formally demanding an investigation into the inaccurate tradelines detailed below. You are legally required to verify these items with the furnishing creditor or remove them within the statutory 30-day investigation window.\n\nI have identified the following specific reporting errors:\n\n1. CREDITOR: CHASE BANK\n   ACCOUNT NUMBER: XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-4321\n   DISCREPANCY IN FIELD: balance (We report: $1200. Other bureaus report: Experian: $1200, Equifax: $1550)\n   REASON FOR DISPUTE: The balance for CHASE BANK is reported inconsistently across credit bureaus. The discrepancy of $350.00 violating FCRA guidelines requiring absolute accuracy in reporting.\n\n2. CREDITOR: CHASE BANK\n   ACCOUNT NUMBER: XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-4321\n   DISCREPANCY IN FIELD: date_opened (We report: 2022-01-15. Other bureaus report: Experian: 2022-01-15, Equifax: 2022-01-17)\n   REASON FOR DISPUTE: The open date for CHASE BANK is reported inconsistently. One bureau reports 2022-01-15 while another reports 2022-01-15. This inaccurate date reporting is a clear violation of FCRA compliance.\n\n3. CREDITOR: CAPITAL ONE\n   ACCOUNT NUMBER: XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-9876\n   DISCREPANCY IN FIELD: payment_status (We report: Late 30 Days. Other bureaus report: Experian: Current, Equifax: Current)\n   REASON FOR DISPUTE: Highly damaging discrepancy: Payment history status for CAPITAL ONE reports \'Late 30 Days\' vs \'Current\'. Payment status must be reported accurately and identically across all reporting bureaus.\n\nPlease send me written confirmation once these corrections have been made. If the furnishing creditors fail to verify the absolute accuracy of these entries within 30 days, you must delete them immediately.\n\nSincerely,\n\n_______________________________\n[Signature]',NULL,NULL,0,NULL,0,NULL,'2026-08-11 12:42:45','2026-08-11 12:42:45',0,NULL,NULL),(2,42,'Experian','Revolving','Multiple','Multiple','Cross-Bureau Discrepancies','Correction or Deletion',1,'Donisha Johnson\n4412 Linecrest Way\nEllenwood, Ga 30294\nDOB: [Enter Date of Birth]\nSSN Last 4: 4187\nPhone: 4703099709\n\nDate: August 11, 2026\n\nTO:\nExperian Credit Services\nCredit Reporting Agency\nATTN: Disputes Department\nPost Office Box 9701\nAllen, TX 75013\n\nRE: NOTICE OF FCRA DISPUTE - INACCURATE REPORTING\n\nDear Disputes Department,\n\nPursuant to the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA), 15 U.S.C. § 1681i (Section 611) and 15 U.S.C. § 1681s-2 (Section 623), I am formally demanding an investigation into the inaccurate tradelines detailed below. You are legally required to verify these items with the furnishing creditor or remove them within the statutory 30-day investigation window.\n\nI have identified the following specific reporting errors:\n\n1. CREDITOR: CHASE BANK\n   ACCOUNT NUMBER: XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-4321\n   DISCREPANCY IN FIELD: balance (We report: $1200. Other bureaus report: TransUnion: $1200, Equifax: $1550)\n   REASON FOR DISPUTE: The balance for CHASE BANK is reported inconsistently across credit bureaus. The discrepancy of $350.00 violating FCRA guidelines requiring absolute accuracy in reporting.\n\n2. CREDITOR: CHASE BANK\n   ACCOUNT NUMBER: XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-4321\n   DISCREPANCY IN FIELD: date_opened (We report: 2022-01-15. Other bureaus report: TransUnion: 2022-01-15, Equifax: 2022-01-17)\n   REASON FOR DISPUTE: The open date for CHASE BANK is reported inconsistently. One